sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XIII — bovid horns as logarithmic spirals wound on a cone (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 53.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Fig. 320 outer edge (550 points, 278 deg sweep) fitted by a free-pole logarithmic spiral: alpha_proj = 85.9 deg, whorl ratio 1.57, Pearson r(ln rho, theta) = 0.91, RMSE 16.7 px (4.6 % of mean radius). Log spiral beats circle (delta-AIC 246) and Archimedean spiral (delta-AIC 12). Thompson's alpha = 75 deg (R = 5.4) is NOT reproduced by the projection (alpha_proj - 75 = +10.9 deg). The v1 verdict logic returns \"refuted\" because both the r >= 0.95 and the |alpha - 75| <= 5 deg criteria fail; that logic ignores the sin(beta) cot(alpha) degeneracy and is itself a Pass-1 defect. Overall 48.9/100. Overall 53.5/100 (faithfulness 46.9, reproducibility 68.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit b0060c02; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 62, Morphological realism / specimen match 35, Parameter expressivity 45, Morphometric validation 48, Source and data traceability 78, Code-to-model traceability 70, Reproducibility package 60. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_031_the_shapes_of_horns_and_of_tee_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-031_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks-with-a.py at b0060c02, image/png, 406769 B, 1760×990 px, artifact_sha256 32b7ee29bfb996ac84fc260284bb464cd4bdc241cdc4cdb4728b0db4b6aca763 (sha256 32b7ee29bfb996ac84fc260284bb464cd4bdc241cdc4cdb4728b0db4b6aca763), spec_fingerprint 78b39928d6410ad23f00651145d4b7faa4e8de550bae97e1a0f3272bacd16b08. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 78b39928d6410ad23f00651145d4b7faa4e8de550bae97e1a0f3272bacd16b08; artifact_sha256: 32b7ee29bfb996ac84fc260284bb464cd4bdc241cdc4cdb4728b0db4b6aca763; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/dryad_qz612jmb4_dataset_Tidiereetal2020.txt=8e13941af7964f2d..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/ovis_ammon_argali_skull_horns_specimen.jpg=f8c17c09c7ebe13e..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/paper_citations.bib=eb8c1ca49ca4877d..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/scout_manifest.json=c6e9d7fbfcf1ea70..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/t1917_031_the_shapes_of_horns_and_of_tee_reference.json=64826ef38cca003b..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/thompson_1917_fig318_ram_horns_diagram.jpg=18f820edfb2de26c..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/thompson_1917_fig319_capra_sinaitica_head.jpg=55131cbad1f81417..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-031/thompson_1917_fig320_ovis_ammon_head.jpg=4d6a6093ce49a70a...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Ovis ammon spiral angle about 75 deg; Highland ram a little more; Scinde wild goat < 70 deg; Oryx 20-40 deg (p. 617) | Argali species share alpha but differ in the cone/helical component beta (pp. 617-618) | trihedral edge lengths 80:74:45 cm (p. 618); St Venant torsion curves on the rings (pp. 621-624); reconstructed_in_script: E1 free-pole log-spiral fit of the outer edge of Fig. 320; AIC vs Archimedean spiral and circle | E2/E3 helico-spiral rendering and whorl-ratio table; gnomonic growth animation; transfer_boundary: a lateral 2D projection measures k_proj = sin(beta) cot(alpha), not alpha itself; does_not_claim: torsion / St Venant warping; inter-species beta differences; anything about teeth or tusks." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Independent second assessor from a different provider — this round is builder-scored'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': \"Analyse the real Ovis ammon specimen photograph (HSV segmentation of the horn sheath) and Thompson's Capra sinaitica figure so that two species and one real specimen are fitted\"}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': \"Add the projection-invariant gnomonic test (E4): inner edge and breadth profile along rays from the fitted pole; compare k_breadth with k_edge; report the implied cone semi-angle beta for Thompson's alpha = 75 deg\"}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Add uncertainty: bootstrap CI on alpha and k, KS test on standardised residuals, relative RMSE; add synthetic positive/negative controls and a shuffled-angle ablation to the measured rows'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Replace the alpha-only verdict logic with one that separates (a) spiral-vs-null model comparison, (b) alpha/beta identifiability and (c) gnomonic self-similarity, and label the Dryad table as a non-shape analogue in the result'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'Trim the mandible junction from the Fig. 320 ventral sector automatically (monotone ln rho criterion) instead of relying on the hand-set sector end'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R7', 'item': \"Render a beta sweep (acute vs blunt cone, Thompson's O. poli vs O. ammon contrast) alongside the alpha sweep\"}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.535"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (builder-assessor, single-agent Pass 1; second assessor pending)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

